README.md-49-## Deployment and security boundary
README.md-50-
README.md:51:See [`deploy/README.md`](deploy/README.md) for the Docker Compose deployment. The stack separates the web proxy, backend, TTS, ASR, and optional LLM services, and stores application data separately from downloaded model files.
README.md-52-
README.md-53-BabyEng is intended for a trusted household network. The backend port is not exposed to the host by default and is reached through Nginx on the Compose network. Do not expose the application directly to the public Internet. Remote access requires HTTPS plus a separate access-control layer, such as a household VPN or authenticated reverse proxy. Recordings, child profile data, learning history, and unmatched questions are sensitive data concerning a minor.
README.md-54-
README.md:55:Inference services are optional at runtime: if TTS or ASR is unavailable or its model is missing, the UI falls back to the text-based learning flow instead of failing the page.
